  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Key team members include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Significant milestones include the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and ongoing efforts to gather stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. Financially, the project has seen various budget approvals: an initial $500,000 for phase one, a $2M executive approval covering R&D and marketing, $55,000 for compliance training and audits, and $15,000 for specialized team training. Detailed budget allocations are to be discussed in the August 1st team meeting."
